From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rust-mos-sync <rust-mos-sync@localhost>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:39:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] codegen_llvm: MOS has no reliable f16/f128

llvm-mos cannot legalize `half` constant materialization ("unable to
legalize instruction: G_FCONSTANT half"), hit while building
compiler_builtins for mos-unknown-none (its f16 add/sub/etc. routines
are only compiled when target_has_reliable_f16 is set). f128 excluded
proactively for the same reason: an immature backend with no native
float support at all.

Unlike the LLVM-version-gated entries this sits next to, this is not a
tracked upstream LLVM bug expected to disappear on the next bump.
---
 compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/llvm_util.rs | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/llvm_util.rs b/compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/llvm_util.rs
index 73b7f699b606dbcfe3d2bbce8a1f6de6836f9672..a2b5b064e66334768adce19dfaab24a65703796c 100644
--- a/compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/llvm_util.rs
+++ b/compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/llvm_util.rs
@@ -367,6 +367,12 @@ fn update_target_reliable_float_cfg(sess: &Session, cfg: &mut TargetConfig) {
     let (major, _, _) = version;
 
     cfg.has_reliable_f16 = match (target_arch, target_os) {
+        // rust-mos-sync: llvm-mos cannot legalize `half` constant materialization
+        // ("unable to legalize instruction: G_FCONSTANT half"). Unlike the
+        // LLVM-version-gated bugs below, this is specific to the young MOS
+        // backend, not a tracked upstream LLVM issue expected to get fixed by
+        // an LLVM bump.
+        (Arch::Mos, _) => false,
         // Unsupported <https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/94434> (fixed in llvm22)
         (Arch::Arm64EC, _) if major < 22 => false,
         // MinGW ABI bugs <https://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=115054>
@@ -385,6 +391,9 @@ fn update_target_reliable_float_cfg(sess: &Session, cfg: &mut TargetConfig) {
     };
 
     cfg.has_reliable_f128 = match (target_arch, target_os) {
+        // rust-mos-sync: not verified to work, and f16 already isn't (see above)
+        // on the same young backend; excluded proactively.
+        (Arch::Mos, _) => false,
         // Unsupported https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/121122
         (Arch::AmdGpu, _) => false,
         // Unsupported <https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/94434>
